# SDLC agents (Cursor)

This repository is a **Cursor** project (not Claude Code).

## Routing

1. Prefer skill **`sdlc-automation-agent`** for multi-step build / sprint / discover / debug.
2. Or invoke a role skill: `solution-architect`, `software-engineer`, `frontend-engineer`, `quality-engineer`, `devops`, `sre`, `security-engineer`, etc.
3. Read stack from `docs/architecture/tech-stack.yaml` or `.sdlc-automation-agent.yaml` → `packs.*` / `verify.*`.
4. Load packs from `packs/languages/{pack}/` and `packs/clouds/{cloud}/`.
5. Canonical role content lives under `agents/{role}/`. Stack skills live under `plugins/*/skills/` and are also linked from `.cursor/skills/`.
6. **Java / Spring Boot:** load `stack-spring` index + topic skills (`rest-api-conventions`, `spring-data-jpa`, `problem-details-rfc9457`, …). See `stack-spring/references/STACK-RULES.md` for precedence.
7. **Vue / Nuxt:** load `stack-vue` (`vue-best-practices`, …) and/or `stack-nuxt` (`nuxt`, `vueuse`, …). Prefer Nuxt skills when `nuxt.config` exists.
8. Do **not** use `new-skills/` — it is not part of this repository.
